      "body": "The conflict drew in Athens and its maritime allies, Sparta and the Peloponnesian League, and many other Greek communities. Pericles initially urged reliance on walls and naval supply rather than a major land battle, but plague struck the crowded city. An uneasy peace gave way to renewed fighting, and the failed Sicilian expedition deepened Athenian losses. With Persian assistance, Sparta developed a fleet and eventually severed Athens’ sea communications.",
