      "summary": "Alexander led Macedonian and allied forces across the straits and opened western Asia Minor after victory at the Granicus.",
      "body": "After succeeding Philip II and suppressing resistance in Greece, Alexander attacked the Achaemenid Empire. In 334 BCE he crossed the Hellespont and visited Ilium, or Troy, where his ceremonies invoked heroic tradition. He then defeated an army of Persian satraps at the Granicus. Many western Anatolian cities opened their gates, and the conqueror began reshaping local governments and fiscal relationships.",
