      "summary": "Scipio and Numidian allies defeated Hannibal in North Africa, leading Carthage to accept a restrictive peace.",
      "body": "When Scipio brought Roman forces into North Africa, Carthage recalled Hannibal from Italy. In the battle associated with Zama, Roman infantry dealt with the elephant attack, while allied cavalry, including the forces of the Numidian king Masinissa, played an important role. Hannibal was defeated, leaving Carthage unable to sustain the war on comparable terms. A peace settlement followed in the next year.",
      "context": "While suffering serious defeats in Italy, Rome had continued contesting Iberia and maritime routes. North African politics also shaped the result. Numidian rulers pursued their own dynastic and territorial interests through alliances, rather than serving merely as passive auxiliaries.",
