      "body": "After winning the civil war, Caesar concentrated military and political authority and accepted the title dictator for life. On 15 March 44 BCE, conspirators including Brutus and Cassius attacked him at a Senate meeting. They claimed to defend the republic against personal rule, but lacked a common government capable of controlling the armies and the city. Antony, Caesar’s heir Octavian, and other commanders competed for his political inheritance.",
