      "body": "After defeating Antony and Cleopatra and taking Egypt, Octavian commanded unrivaled military resources. In 27 BCE he proclaimed a restoration of the republic while receiving long-term authority over crucial provinces and the honorific name Augustus. Later settlements added and clarified his powers. Military command, tribunician authority, wealth, and patronage sustained his position. The Senate and republican offices survived, but no longer supported equal competition for supreme power.",
