      "summary": "The eruption buried Pompeii and neighboring settlements, leaving exceptional evidence for reconstructing Roman urban life.",
      "body": "In 79 CE, successive eruptions of Vesuvius covered Campanian settlements with volcanic material. Houses, shops, streets, and public buildings at Pompeii were buried, while Herculaneum and nearby villas suffered different patterns of destruction. Residents attempted to flee, shelter, or assist others, and many died. Buildings, paintings, objects, and writing preserve remarkable evidence, but they represent only part of the city’s experience of the disaster.",
