      "summary": "Diocletian shared authority among two senior and two junior emperors to improve frontier command and the transfer of power.",
      "body": "After taking power in 284, Diocletian confronted war, instability, and fiscal strain by gradually sharing authority. In 293 the system comprised two Augusti, Diocletian and Maximian, and two Caesars, Galerius and Constantius. They supervised different military regions from residences closer to the frontiers. Nicomedia was a major center for Diocletian, while the empire remained formally a single political community.",
