      "outcome": "Later histories commonly use 476 to mark the western empire’s end, while ancient cultural traditions and medieval political forms overlapped for centuries. Roman law, Latin culture and Christian institutions persisted. The eastern empire remained a Roman state, and Italy’s cities and local societies adapted to new kings and further wars.",
