      "body": "After the Nika revolt destroyed the earlier church in 532, Justinian ordered its reconstruction under Anthemios of Tralles and Isidoros of Miletos. A vast central dome, semi-domes and arches organized the interior, where marble decoration and light shaped a major setting for worship and ceremony. The dedication took place on 27 December 537. The project also demonstrated the resources available to an emperor rebuilding the capital after violent destruction.",
