      "context": "Hagia Sophia was the capital’s cathedral, on a site occupied by successive earlier churches. Religious policy, court ritual and urban public life were closely connected, giving Justinian’s reconstruction spiritual, political and engineering significance.",
      "outcome": "The building influenced later religious architecture and underwent repeated repair. Its first dome collapsed in 558 and was rebuilt higher, followed by later reinforcement. Conversion into a mosque after 1453 and changing rituals, uses and decoration added further layers to the monument.",
