      "year": 711,
      "title": "A Political Turning Point in Iberia",
      "city": "gibraltar",
      "category": "政权",
      "summary": "Muslim forces crossed from North Africa as Visigothic royal power collapsed; warfare and local agreements together established al-Andalus.",
      "body": "Tariq led an army with a substantial Berber component across the strait and defeated the forces of the Visigothic king Roderick before advancing inland. Musa brought further troops. Warfare, surrender and agreements with local elites extended control over large areas. The new territories, called al-Andalus, initially belonged to the Umayyad caliphate’s political system. Conquest and local administration developed over several years, with unconquered areas surviving in the north.",
