      "body": "During the Christmas liturgy in Old St Peter’s, Pope Leo III crowned Charlemagne emperor. Charlemagne already ruled extensive Frankish and Italian territories through conquest and had intervened in Roman ecclesiastical politics. The ceremony combined military power, papal approval and Roman imperial precedent, giving Frankish rule a new symbolic form. Coronation and acclamation also made Rome an important setting for the public expression of western imperial authority.",
