      "body": "After Charlemagne’s son Louis the Pious died, Lothar, Louis the German and Charles the Bald contested their father’s inheritance. Warfare, alliances and negotiations produced an agreement in 843. Charles received the western lands, Louis the eastern lands, and Lothar retained the imperial title and a middle realm stretching from the North Sea toward Italy. The settlement accommodated dynastic interests across territories containing diverse local traditions and aristocratic powers.",
