      "body": "Legates sent by Pope Leo IX failed to resolve disputes over authority and worship with Patriarch Michael Cerularius. In 1054 they placed a document of excommunication against the patriarch and his supporters in Hagia Sophia. The patriarch’s side in turn condemned the legates. These censures had specific targets and disputed legal implications; they did not constitute a single formal agreement separating every Christian in east and west.",
