      "summary": "Urban II’s appeal at Clermont joined religious vows to military mobilization, helping launch the First Crusade.",
      "body": "During the council at Clermont, Pope Urban II called on western Christians to march east, linking aid to Byzantium with religious goals in the Holy Land and offering spiritual benefits to participants. Bishops, nobles and preachers spread the appeal, while volunteers took vows and adopted the cross. Surviving versions of the speech were written later and emphasize different motives and themes. Urban’s contemporary letters also show how the papacy sought to organize the expedition.",
