      "context": "Byzantium faced Turkish pressure in Asia Minor and its emperor sought western assistance. Latin Church reform, pilgrimage traditions and the military practices of knightly society provided conditions in which the pope could present an armed expedition as a religious undertaking.",
      "outcome": "Different contingents departed from 1096, and the First Crusade captured Jerusalem in 1099 and established Latin territories. Mobilization also brought violence against Jewish communities in Europe and devastating warfare for eastern Mediterranean inhabitants. Relations between Latin and Greek Christians were reshaped as well.",
