      "city": "runnymede",
      "category": "制度",
      "summary": "A settlement between the king and rebellious barons limited royal power at Runnymede; its failed peace terms acquired a lasting legal legacy.",
      "body": "Military failures, taxation, and disputes over justice intensified conflict between John and leading barons. After rebels took London, negotiations at Runnymede produced a charter accepted in June 1215 and authenticated with the royal seal. Its provisions addressed feudal obligations, church and civic liberties, taxation, and legal procedure, with a baronial enforcement mechanism. It was a political compromise, not a grant of modern equal rights to all inhabitants.",
