      "locationNote": "Runnymede lies beside the Thames between Windsor and Staines. The 1215 sealing is located to the meadow area.",
      "context": "Medieval government relied on negotiated relationships among the king, church, nobles, and towns, and written charters were familiar instruments. John’s fiscal and military policies strained those relationships. The document therefore answered particular grievances within a society unlike one of modern citizenship.",
      "outcome": "The peace soon failed, the pope annulled the charter, and civil war continued. Revised versions issued in 1216, 1217, and 1225 preserved parts of it. Later generations repeatedly reinterpreted the text, associating it increasingly with lawful government and limits on arbitrary authority.",
