      "id": "joan-1429",
      "year": 1429,
      "title": "The Relief of Orléans",
      "city": "orleans",
      "category": "战争",
      "summary": "French forces relieved Orléans, and Joan’s participation strengthened morale before the advance to Reims renewed support for Charles VII’s kingship.",
      "body": "English troops had besieged Orléans since 1428, using fortified positions to control access around the city and along the Loire. With support from Charles VII’s court, Joan entered on 29 April 1429 and joined existing commanders and defenders. French attacks captured outlying positions in early May and the important bridgehead works on 7 May, when Joan was wounded. The English withdrew on 8 May, reopening access to the city as further French operations continued along the Loire.",
