      "body": "Several provinces participating in the Dutch Revolt adopted a declaration that Philip II had forfeited his authority through oppression. It described a prince as a protector of subjects rather than their owner and listed abuses attributed to Spanish rule. The measure formed part of the struggle associated with William of Orange and other opponents of the crown. Its supporters initially still sought a replacement sovereign, rather than immediately establishing the republic in its later form.",
