      "summary": "The Armada failed to join the invasion army in the Netherlands; fighting, logistical problems and storms together shaped the defeat.",
      "body": "Philip II sent a fleet under the duke of Medina Sidonia to escort the duke of Parma’s army across from the Netherlands. English ships harassed it along the Channel. Fireships forced the Armada from its anchorage off Calais, followed by fighting near Gravelines. The planned junction and invasion failed. The fleet sailed north around Britain and suffered further losses from shortages, damage and severe weather during its return voyage.",
