      "summary": "Bohemian Protestant nobles threw royal officials from a castle window, turning a constitutional and religious dispute into open rebellion.",
      "body": "Protestant nobles entered Prague Castle, accused royal officials of violating religious rights and threw two governors and a secretary from a window. All three survived, but the action marked open rebellion. The insurgents established a provisional government, later rejected Habsburg Ferdinand and elected another king. Dynastic, princely and foreign intervention gradually carried the conflict beyond Bohemia.",
      "context": "Disputes concerned the interpretation of guarantees of religious liberty, the closure of Protestant churches and relations between the estates and the crown. Ferdinand was already king of Bohemia but was not yet emperor in May 1618. The crisis cannot be reduced to one imperial command demanding immediate universal conversion.",
