      "body": "Charles I raised his standard at Nottingham in 1642 as royalists and parliamentarians entered sustained warfare. Parliament later created the New Model Army and gained major victories, including Naseby. Military success did not resolve divisions among the army, Parliament and the king. Renewed fighting encouraged radicalization and helped lead to the trial and execution of Charles in 1649. Republican campaigns in Ireland and Scotland followed, making this a conflict extending beyond England.",
