      "body": "On 24 October 1648 the core imperial treaties with France and Sweden were signed in Münster after separate negotiating tracks in Münster and Osnabrück. The Osnabrück treaty retained the name of its negotiating city. The agreements restored or revised territorial rights, settled land and compensation claims and recognized the Reformed confession within imperial religious law. The year 1624 became a benchmark for many questions of religious property and practice. An earlier Spanish–Dutch Treaty of Münster separately recognized Dutch independence. These connected but distinct instruments form the wider Peace of Westphalia.",
