      "summary": "A court authorized by a reduced Parliament condemned Charles I, followed by the temporary abolition of monarchy and the House of Lords.",
      "body": "After renewed civil war, the army excluded members of Parliament who opposed trying the king. The remaining Commons authorized a special court. Charles I denied its jurisdiction, while the court convicted him of waging war against his people. He was beheaded outside the Banqueting House at Whitehall on 30 January. Regicide reflected decisions by the army and part of Parliament, not unanimous parliamentary or national agreement.",
