      "summary": "After the collapse of the Protectorate, Charles II returned to London as monarchy, the Lords and the established church were restored.",
      "body": "Oliver Cromwell’s death exposed the Protectorate’s weak succession arrangements and renewed struggles between the army and Parliament. General George Monck brought troops south and helped create conditions for elections. The Convention Parliament invited Charles II to return. In the Declaration of Breda, Charles offered conditional pardon and promised arrangements for outstanding disputes. His entry into London on 29 May became the emblematic moment of restoration.",
