      "summary": "A London group for experimental natural philosophy developed institutions for demonstrations, correspondence and the publication of results.",
      "body": "After a lecture by Christopher Wren at Gresham College, a group interested in natural knowledge agreed to meet regularly for observation and experiment. It became the Royal Society and received a royal charter in 1662. Robert Hooke organized experiments, while Henry Oldenburg managed correspondence and began Philosophical Transactions in 1665. These practices enabled dispersed findings to be reported, compared and challenged.",
