      "summary": "John III Sobieski and imperial forces defeated the Ottoman besiegers, opening a major shift in Habsburg–Ottoman relations.",
      "body": "Grand Vizier Kara Mustafa’s Ottoman army besieged Vienna while its defenders resisted through fortifications, trenches and mining operations. A relief force combining King John III Sobieski of Poland with contingents from the Holy Roman Empire attacked from the surrounding heights on 12 September and forced the besiegers to retreat. Allied cooperation, sustained defence and battlefield conditions mattered alongside the famous cavalry assault.",
      "context": "Ottoman and Habsburg power had long competed across Hungary and the central European frontier. Local political and religious struggles interacted with Ottoman support for opponents of Habsburg rule. Vienna was a major dynastic centre, but cooperation among European states required diplomacy and resources rather than following an automatic religious unity.",
