      "body": "The Edict of Fontainebleau revoked the principal guarantees of the Edict of Nantes of 1598. It ordered the destruction of Protestant places of worship, ended Protestant religious education and required ministers who refused conversion to leave. Ordinary Protestant subjects were generally forbidden to emigrate; the law did not freely offer everyone a choice between conversion and exile. Earlier restrictions and coercive military billeting had already produced numerous nominal conversions.",
