      "body": "William III and Mary II gave royal assent on 16 December 1689, turning the Declaration of Rights presented in February into statute. The act rejected claims to suspend laws, levy taxation or maintain a standing army in peacetime without parliamentary consent. It protected free elections and speech within parliamentary proceedings and condemned excessive bail and cruel punishments. It also settled succession and defended a Protestant political order, making it both a restraint on power and a legal foundation for the new monarchy.",
