      "outcome": "The act strengthened Parliament in finance, legislation and government while retaining substantial restrictions on political participation. Voting remained restricted by property, gender and local institutions, while Catholics continued to face exclusions. Budgets, military administration, cabinet government and succession evolved through later laws and practice. The “1688” year used in the modern statute title does not alter the documented royal-assent date in 1689.",
