      "title": "The Estates General opens",
      "summary": "Louis XVI summoned the Estates General over the fiscal crisis; debate over taxation became a struggle over representation and sovereignty.",
      "body": "Deputies of the clergy, nobility, and Third Estate assembled at Versailles for the first Estates General since 1614. Louis XVI and finance minister Jacques Necker hoped to obtain support for dealing with the deficit. Although the Third Estate had more deputies, voting separately by estate threatened to leave it outvoted by the other two orders. Lists of grievances brought taxation, justice, and political reform into the chamber, carrying debate beyond the crown’s immediate financial plans.",
