      "body": "During the Consulate, civil laws drafted by jurists and debated in the Council of State were consolidated as the Civil Code of the French. Napoleon participated in discussions and drove promulgation. The code organized personal status, property, and ways of acquiring property, reducing the fragmentation of regional customs and older law. It preserved important revolutionary attacks on status privilege while establishing unequal rules within marriage and the family; it was not a universal grant of legal equality.",
