      "summary": "Napoleon’s multinational army advanced deep into Russia; supply failures, disease, combat, and severe cold destroyed the campaign.",
      "body": "In June, Napoleon led French and allied European forces across the Niemen to compel Alexander I to accept French predominance. Russian withdrawals stretched the invaders’ supply lines. After the bloody battle of Borodino in September, the army occupied Moscow, where evacuation and fire greatly reduced the value of its gains. The tsar refused to negotiate. During the retreat from October, Russian attacks, depleted supplies, disease, and worsening cold further weakened the army, which suffered additional losses crossing the Berezina.",
