      "summary": "The railway demonstrated new possibilities for steam-hauled coal and passengers while retaining horses and stationary haulage in regular operation.",
      "body": "Edward Pease and other investors promoted a route from the Durham coalfield to the River Tees, with George Stephenson developing the route and steam-traction scheme. On opening day, Locomotion No. 1 hauled goods and passengers through Darlington toward Stockton. Early operation combined steam-hauled freight, stationary haulage on inclines, and passenger coaches operated by contractors using horses. More integrated management developed gradually.",
