      "summary": "Three days of barricade fighting overthrew Charles X and brought Louis-Philippe to a monarchy with a restricted electorate.",
      "body": "Charles X’s July Ordinances restricted the press, dissolved the newly elected chamber, and narrowed electoral qualifications. Journalists, workers, students, and other Parisians resisted. Barricade fighting from 27 to 29 July cost the crown control of the capital. Liberal politicians then supported Louis-Philippe, duke of Orléans, as “king of the French,” revising the charter rather than establishing a republic.",
