      "body": "The Communist League commissioned Marx and Engels to draft its program, printed in German in London in 1848. They portrayed modern capitalism as expanding production and global connections while generating class antagonism, and linked proletarian organization to social revolution. The work emerged from networks of exiles, artisans, and socialists. Its immediate influence on the revolutions of 1848 was limited; translations, workers’ organizations, and later political debates gave it a much wider readership.",
