      "body": "Disputes over religious protection in Ottoman territory and Russia’s occupation of the Danubian principalities escalated into an Ottoman declaration of war in October 1853. Britain and France entered in 1854, landed in Crimea, and besieged Russia’s Black Sea naval base at Sevastopol; Sardinia joined in 1855. Battles at the Alma, Balaklava, and Inkerman accompanied a prolonged siege marked by disease and transport failures. Russian forces evacuated the southern part of the city in September 1855, and peace negotiations followed in Paris in 1856.",
