      "outcome": "The Treaty of Paris restricted Russia’s military position in the Black Sea, while the conflict weakened the great-power cooperation established after Vienna. Defeat encouraged domestic reform under Alexander II. British failures in hospitals and supply stimulated changes in sanitation and military administration, with Nightingale and others drawing attention to nursing and statistical evidence.",
