      "body": "The German High Seas Fleet sought to lure out and destroy part of the British fleet, while intelligence helped Britain send its Grand Fleet to sea. Battle cruisers under Franz von Hipper and David Beatty engaged first, followed by the main fleets under Reinhard Scheer and John Jellicoe. Daylight gunnery and night actions inflicted losses on both sides before the Germans returned to base. The battle ranged across the North Sea rather than taking place on Danish land.",
