      "body": "Douglas Haig sought to advance from the Ypres salient, seize the ridges and threaten the German-held Belgian coast. British and French forces opened the offensive in late July, followed by repeated commitments of British, Australian, New Zealand and Canadian formations. Shellfire destroyed drainage and rain turned the ground into mud, obstructing supply, evacuation and artillery movement. Canadians captured Passchendaele village on 6 November, with further fighting for nearby heights afterwards.",
