      "body": "On 21 March, Operation Michael struck British positions near Saint-Quentin. Concentrated bombardment and infiltration by assault troops produced a major breakthrough. Ludendorff followed with further attacks in Flanders, on the Aisne and elsewhere, restoring large movements to the Western Front. Britain and France rearranged their forces as Foch gained authority to coordinate Allied action. German gains created expanding salients, stretched supply lines and depleted experienced assault formations.",
