      "outcome": "Germany achieved striking advances but failed to separate Britain and France or compel peace. Heavy losses and logistical difficulties weakened further attacks. After the reversal on the Marne in July, the initiative increasingly passed to a succession of Allied counteroffensives.",
      "locationNote": "Saint-Quentin identifies an important sector of Operation Michael. The successive spring and summer offensives ranged much farther across Flanders, the Aisne and the Marne.",
      "sortOrder": 321
