      "body": "On 15 July, German armies attacked on both sides of Reims in an effort to improve their position and sustain pressure on France. French defence in depth weakened the assault while Allied troops resisted at river crossings and communications points. On 18 July, a counteroffensive coordinated by Foch struck the salient, notably from the west. French and American formations played major roles alongside other Allied troops. The Germans abandoned positions south of the Marne and withdrew.",
