      "outcome": "Germany failed to recover the strategic initiative. The Allies regained ground and moved towards a sustained sequence of offensives, but Amiens and the Hundred Days were still needed to consolidate the advantage. This was neither a battle that ended the war by itself nor the victory of a single nation.",
