      "body": "On 30 January 1933, President Paul von Hindenburg appointed Nazi leader Adolf Hitler chancellor. Franz von Papen and other conservative politicians helped arrange the coalition, believing they could contain him. The Nazis were the largest party in parliament but had won no majority in a free national election; voters had not directly elected Hitler chancellor. The new government immediately combined executive authority, propaganda and paramilitary violence against opponents, then used emergency decrees and the Enabling Act to build a dictatorship.",
