      "body": "After breaking through near Sedan, German forces reached the Channel and cut off the British Expeditionary Force and parts of the French and Belgian armies. Operation Dynamo began on 26 May. Warships, transports and civilian craft worked within a naval operation to evacuate about 338,000 Allied troops from Dunkirk’s harbor and beaches under air and artillery attack. French and other rearguards helped maintain the perimeter, while much heavy equipment and many vehicles had to be abandoned.",
