      "body": "On 8 September 1941, German capture of Shlisselburg cut Leningrad’s principal land connection to the Soviet interior, while Finnish forces exerted pressure from the north. Food rations collapsed, heating and transport failed, and artillery and air attacks continued. Shipping across Lake Ladoga and winter ice roads sustained limited supply and evacuation. Repeated Soviet offensives eventually opened a narrow land corridor in January 1943; the siege was fully lifted only in January 1944.",
