      "summary": "Sixteen European countries met in Paris to develop a joint recovery programme in response to the American aid proposal.",
      "body": "After Marshall’s June speech in the United States, Britain and France encouraged European governments to prepare common requirements. Representatives of sixteen countries discussed shortages of production, food, energy and foreign exchange in Paris and signed the Committee of European Economic Cooperation report on 22 September. The Soviet Union rejected this framework, and most eastern European states did not join. Congress authorized aid the following year, allowing money and supplies to flow through the European Recovery Program.",
