      "body": "Following the Moscow Treaty of 12 August, Chancellor Willy Brandt and Foreign Minister Walter Scheel travelled to Warsaw and signed a treaty normalizing relations with Poland. The parties committed to existing borders, territorial integrity and non-use of force. Brandt’s kneeling at the Warsaw Ghetto memorial became a powerful image of historical responsibility. The treaties provoked intense parliamentary controversy in West Germany and were ratified in 1972.",
