      "summary": "Voters in the nine Community states directly elected MEPs for the first time; the new Parliament then chose Simone Veil as president.",
      "body": "In June the nine European Community states elected Members of the European Parliament through their national electoral procedures, replacing delegation by national parliaments. MEPs organized into transnational political groups. The new Parliament subsequently met in Strasbourg and elected French politician Simone Veil as president. Direct election strengthened representation, although Parliament’s legislative powers remained much narrower than those granted by later treaties.",
