      "body": "Strikes over prices and working conditions spread across Poland. Shipyard workers in Gdańsk and an inter-factory strike committee coordinated demands, with Lech Wałęsa among the leading negotiators. The agreement signed on 31 August recognized rights to independent unions and strikes, enabling Solidarity’s formation. Workers, intellectuals and church supporters cooperated, although the movement encompassed differing ambitions and political views.",
