      "bio": "Pétain gained prestige through his organisation of transport, artillery and troop rotation in the Verdun defence. In 1917 he replaced Nivelle as French commander in chief, improving soldiers’ conditions while restoring discipline and punishing mutineers. After France’s defeat in 1940, he headed the Vichy regime, dismantled republican government and pursued collaboration with Nazi Germany. The regime enacted its own antisemitic laws and participated in persecution and deportation. Convicted of treason in 1945, he received a death sentence that was commuted to life imprisonment; he died in 1951.",
